  "elements": [
    {
      "id": "R9GJZmFoCZcBNxfzED6Z7",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 445.98046875,
      "y": 113.234375,
      "width": 897.3125000000001,
      "height": 1875,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bCz",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 828700187,
      "version": 1758,
      "versionNonce": 760159093,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1742975593065,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Design live comments feature on streaming platforms\n\nFunctional requirements:\n1. User can post comments on a live stream video\n2. User can view live comments\n3. User can view past comments before they joined the stream\n\nScale:\n1M streams per day\n100 comments on each video\n\nNon functional requirements:\n1. Scalability -> for upload and reading of live comments\n2. High availability >> consistency\n3. Eventual consistency for showing comments\n4. Low latency (< 500ms)\n\nBack of the envelope calculation:\n\n1. Throughput\n\nread: \nassumption: 1: 100 ratio\n12000k TPS\n\nwrite: \nassumption: each video is 1 hour on average\n1M * 100 * 24 -> 24 * 10^8 / 10^5 ~ 24k TPS ~ 120k TPS\n\nCore entities:\n\n1. VideoMetadata\n2. User\nuserId: UUID\nname\ndob: timestamp\nisActive: boolean\n\n3. Comment\ncommentId: UUID\nvideoId: FK, VideoMetadata\nuserId: FK, User\ncontent: varchar(200)\ncreatedAt: timestamp\n\nAPIs:\n\n1. POST /api/v1/video/{videoId}/comment\n200: success\n400: bad status\n500\n404: video id does not exist\n\nRequest body ->\n{\n    \"content\": \"\"\n}\n\nResponse ->\n{\n    \"commentId\": \"\",\n}\n\n2. GET /api/v1/video/{videoId}/comments?page=1&limit=50&direction={\"past\" | \"new\"}\n\nResponse -> \n{\n    \"data\": [{\n        \"commentId\": \"\",\n        \"content\": \"\",\n        \"createdAt': \"\"\n    }]\n}\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Design live comments feature on streaming platforms\n\nFunctional requirements:\n1. User can post comments on a live stream video\n2. User can view live comments\n3. User can view past comments before they joined the stream\n\nScale:\n1M streams per day\n100 comments on each video\n\nNon functional requirements:\n1. Scalability -> for upload and reading of live comments\n2. High availability >> consistency\n3. Eventual consistency for showing comments\n4. Low latency (< 500ms)\n\nBack of the envelope calculation:\n\n1. Throughput\n\nread: \nassumption: 1: 100 ratio\n12000k TPS\n\nwrite: \nassumption: each video is 1 hour on average\n1M * 100 * 24 -> 24 * 10^8 / 10^5 ~ 24k TPS ~ 120k TPS\n\nCore entities:\n\n1. VideoMetadata\n2. User\nuserId: UUID\nname\ndob: timestamp\nisActive: boolean\n\n3. Comment\ncommentId: UUID\nvideoId: FK, VideoMetadata\nuserId: FK, User\ncontent: varchar(200)\ncreatedAt: timestamp\n\nAPIs:\n\n1. POST /api/v1/video/{videoId}/comment\n200: success\n400: bad status\n500\n404: video id does not exist\n\nRequest body ->\n{\n    \"content\": \"\"\n}\n\nResponse ->\n{\n    \"commentId\": \"\",\n}\n\n2. GET /api/v1/video/{videoId}/comments?page=1&limit=50&direction={\"past\" | \"new\"}\n\nResponse -> \n{\n    \"data\": [{\n        \"commentId\": \"\",\n        \"content\": \"\",\n        \"createdAt': \"\"\n    }]\n}\n\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
